#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
iherb - agent-native CLI for iHerb Taiwan (tw.iherb.com, TWD). No checkout.

Zero dependencies (Python 3.8+ stdlib). Every command supports --json and
returns the {ok, data|error} envelope used by the other ~/Projects CLIs.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 api, 2 usage, 3 auth, 4 net/blocked.

Endpoints, measured 2026-10-29 with real requests
--------------------------------------------------
Search (HTML, plain HTTPS works, no cookie needed):
  GET https://tw.iherb.com/search?kw=<q>&sr=<sort>&p=<page>
      48 `div.product-cell-container` per page: data-product-id, data-part-number,
      data-ga-brand-name, title, span.price / span.price-olp / .percentage-off,
      rating title '4.8/5 - 492,573 評論', data-is-out-of-stock, #product-count.
      sr: 13 精選(default) 0 relevance 2 bestselling 1 rating 12 reviews
          4 price low->high 3 price high->low 10 newest 14 discount
      CAVEAT (measured 2026-10-30, confirmed on the live site): some listings on
      every sort/page render with no price at all - discontinued items
      (data-ga-is-discontinued="True") and items iHerb blocks from purchase in this
      region/account, shown with "無法購買" (cannot purchase) + a "查看類似商品" link
      instead of a price span. Both are genuinely not purchasable, so the CLI drops
      any search result with price=None (see parse_search()/cmd_search()); the
      remaining real prices on a --sort price/price-desc page were verified already
      in sorted order once those are removed, so no client-side re-sort is needed.
      --min/--max/--limit/--page still apply only to the single remote page fetched
      (see below), now over this cleaned pool.
Catalog GraphQL (JSON, plain HTTPS; Cloudflare sometimes challenges cookieless
bursts, a saved session's cf_clearance passes):
  POST https://graphql-catalog.app.iherb.com/?country=TW&currency=TWD&language=zh-TW
      products(input:{ids:[...]}) { label productName brand url inventory
      calculatedPrice{price{discount list discountPercentage} discounts{publicPCode}}
      ugc{reviews} groupingAttributes ... }    -> product / price
      freeShippingThreshold{amount{formatted}}  -> shipping line
Product page (HTML): GET https://tw.iherb.com/pr/<slug>/<id>
      Cloudflare 403 without cookies; 200 over plain HTTP with the saved session
      cookies (cf_clearance) + the Edge User-Agent they were issued to. Holds the
      variant tiles: div.product-grouping-row[data-testid=product-grouping-row-<名>]
      > .attribute-tile/.thumbnail-tile [data-val, data-pid, data-is-out-of-stock].
      On iHerb a variant IS another product id. Without a session: CDP fallback.
Account (cookies .iHerbAuth.Cookies / .AuthServer.Cookies on .iherb.com):
  GET  https://catalog.app.iherb.com/catalog/currentUser   200 {id,email,welcomeName,
       rewardsCode,registrationDate} signed in, 401 not
  POST https://checkout8.iherb.com/account/isloggedin {"requestUrl":"/"}
       -> {status, expirationMs}
Cart (checkout8, headers Pref:{"lac":"zh-TW","ctc":"TW","crc":"TWD","crs":"0"},
CustomerId:<user id>; works over plain HTTP with the saved cookies):
  GET    /api/Carts/v2/cartcount            {totalQuantity,...}
  GET    /api/Carts/v2                      full cart: lineItems, subTotal, cartTotal..
  POST   /api/Carts/v3/catalog/lineItems    {"lineItems":[{"productId","quantity",
         "frequencyId":null}],"sourceModule":"ProductDetailsPage",...}  add
  PUT    /api/Carts/v2/lineitem             {"productId","quantity"}         set qty
  DELETE /api/Carts/v2/lineitems/products   {"lineItems":[pid],"sourceModule":"CartLists"}
Captured from Edge's own traffic (CDP Network domain, background tab).
Lightpanda 1.0.2 `fetch` renders the product page too, but in English (no
locale), so it is not used. Never called: /checkout, /api/checkout*, orders.

Login: never passwords/OTP. `iherb login` (default --from-browser) reads the
cookies of the Edge on IHERB_CDP; if not signed in it opens the iHerb sign-in
page in a background tab and polls until you sign in there. The session is
verified with currentUser over plain HTTP before it is saved to
~/.config/iherb/state.json (0600) or the OS keyring (--keyring; chunked, since
secret-tool lookup returns at most 8192 bytes and the session is ~10 KB). IHERB_COOKIE
(a Cookie header) overrides both. Cart commands use only that saved session.

Unofficial. Undocumented, private API - it can break without warning.
"""
